{
	"Name": "ScheduledSearch - Okta - User - Authentication - Okta Max Sign-In Attempts Exceeded [table]",
	"Description": "Counts sign-ins Okta refused because the account had already hit the sign-on policy's attempt limit. Unlike a lockout event this fires on every attempt after the limit, so it shows how long something kept trying after Okta started refusing.\n\nThreshold: 3 or more refusals per account. Edit the eval near the end of the query to tune it.\n\nThis detection uses stats, so it renders as a table rather than shipping raw entries.\n\nReference(s):\n- https://support.okta.com/help/s/article/User-Signin-and-Recovery-Events-in-the-Okta-System-Log\n- https://developer.okta.com/docs/reference/api/event-types/\n\nThis scheduled search is a dispatcher on \"Alert - Okta - Alert Router\". Its name is what appears as the alert name, so rename it here if you want the alerts named differently.\n\nIt ships disabled; enable it once you have reviewed the query and are happy with the volume it produces.",
	"Labels": [
		"okta"
	],
	"Schedule": "*/15 * * * *",
	"Duration": -900,
	"DefaultDeploymentRules": {
		"Disabled": true,
		"RunImmediately": false
	},
	"ScheduledType": "search",
	"GUID": "9147105a-e60e-5cbf-9936-0b809f95dd5c",
	"SearchReference": "a34f27b7-edf8-55cc-926f-eb5226e9eba5"
}